            <div class="post">
                <div class="posthead">
                    <h2><a href="/blogs/ryanc/archive/2008/07/31/why-plain-old-linq-is-so-powerful.aspx">Why Plain Old LINQ is so powerful</a></h2>
                    Posted 
                    <a href="/blogs/ryanc/archive/2008/07/31/why-plain-old-linq-is-so-powerful.aspx">Thursday, July 31, 2008 5:04 PM</a>                
                    by
					<a href="/members/cromwellryan/default.aspx">cromwellryan</a> 
                </div>

               <p><a href="http://www.interact-sw.co.uk/iangblog/" target="_blank">Ian Griffiths</a> posted a <a href="http://www.interact-sw.co.uk/iangblog/2008/07/30/linq-box-aggregation" target="_blank">great example</a> of how powerful and cool LINQ is when used in everyday code (it&#39;s not all about databases people).</p> <p>If you haven&#39;t started to learn how to incorporate this awesome toolset into your daily coding life, you&#39;re killing yourself.&nbsp; No excuses.</p><div style="clear:both;"></div>

                <div class="postfoot">	
                    
                            with <a href="/blogs/ryanc/archive/2008/07/31/why-plain-old-linq-is-so-powerful.aspx#comments">2 comment(s)</a>
                            
                         
                    
                    
                    <div class="em"><span id="ctl00_Main_EntryItems_ctl06_InlineTagEditorPanel_ctl01">Filed under: <a href="/blogs/ryanc/archive/tags/.Net/default.aspx" rel="tag">.Net</a></span><input type="hidden" name="ctl00$Main$EntryItems$ctl06$InlineTagEditorPanel$ctl01" id="ctl00_Main_EntryItems_ctl06_InlineTagEditorPanel_ctl01_State" value="nochange" /></div>                    
                   
