					<a href="/members/cromwellryan/default.aspx">cromwellryan</a> 
                </div>

               <p>If you are running a VPC instance and you&#39;d like to take a screenshot of something on the VPC, did you know you can do that without any photo editing hassle?</p> <p>Simply make sure you aren&#39;t &quot;in&quot; the VPC (hit the right Alt key if you are).&nbsp; Now click and drag a square around the portion of the VM you want to capture.&nbsp; CTRL+C or Edit -&gt; Copy will capture the section to the clipboard and you can paste it wherever.&nbsp; </p> <p>Nice touch.</p><div style="clear:both;"></div>

